	(text ""
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 240.792 71.374 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "93ec7fb5-a965-459f-a4b3-4a37e517cd92")
	)
	(text_box "R1 selected to give max charging current of ~1A (nominal value recommended by the battery datasheet, can go up to 2A)\nVSET sets the charging voltage (8.4V). A >150kOhm value is recommended for R2. The pin can also be left floating.\nR9 has the value recommended by the datasheet.\nR9 = 383Ohm -> IIN max = 2.9A"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 67.31 68.58 0)
		(size 48.26 20.3201)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2c3d501c-604c-4e55-8016-06f40bfba605")
	)
	(text_box "This bloc is the external connection of the battery to the board. It is not to be mistaken with the CHAR/BATT1 connector used to perform tests on the circuit without unplugging the battery. We use a JST PH connector to give the user the opportunity to plug and unplug the battery."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 59.69 111.0632 0)
		(size 66.04 12.1268)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 92 0 255 0.168627451)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "31168909-10f9-44ff-be8f-b73721645020")
	)
	(text_box "BATTERY CONNECTION\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 91.44 0)
		(size 97.79 31.75)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3e3871e3-5c50-44b5-88bf-165b8a569554")
	)
	(text_box "Sets the different values necessary for the proper function of the IC. Sets the charging values of the battery."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 238.76 76.7732 0)
		(size 29.21 12.1268)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 92 0 255 0.168627451)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4cd332ba-a756-4d6c-b668-de44ca35fa79")
	)
	(text_box "CHARGING IC - SETUP\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 21.59 0)
		(size 240.03 67.31)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "721cd03c-e0c9-4b89-9db6-290117bba8d5")
	)
	(text_box "Handles the charging of the battery and power management of the system. To understand the function of each pin, please refer to the documentation, as most of the connections, resistor and capacitance value selection has been done by following the requirements/recommendations of the datasheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 222.25 144.7799 0)
		(size 45.72 19.0501)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 92 0 255 0.168627451)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9ac59d2f-fb11-41a8-a2a6-7a65f3d01b28")
	)
	(text_box "CHARGING IC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 129.54 88.9 0)
		(size 138.43 74.93)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9eedbe52-46c9-4065-816c-1cfb5c385cb4")
	)
	(text_box "R14 is a thermistor to be placed as close to the battery as possible. The Seiko BMS integrated in our battery only handles the electric protection (charge, discharge) and not the temperature. Via TS, the IC progressively adjusts the charging profile according to the temperature to preserve the battery (JEITA). Its value at 25°C should be of 10kOhm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 38.61 0)
		(size 38.1 22.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c6e3b142-60a9-4877-a1b1-fac0922d59c3")
	)
	(text_box "USB-C CONNECTOR\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 124.46 0)
		(size 97.79 68.58)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c8af01fa-6292-4fd6-9acc-319a4d8825fd")
	)
	(text_box "The USB connector we use has to be compatible with the IC used to manage the battery. This is why we chose a USB-C 2.0 connector. The wiring is done to turn it into a \"dumb\" charger, providing the IC with the information of how much current and voltage it can pull, charging the battery and powering the system if a cable is connected, ignoring most of its data transfer abilities."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 87.63 166.5861 0)
		(size 38.1 26.4392)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 92 0 255 0.168627451)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d425b8e8-f8b9-4d84-b1ad-bbbe188df713")
	)
	(text_box "L2: power inductor\nIRIPPLE = VBUS × (VSYS − VBUS) / (VSYS × fSW × L) = 1.35A \nVBUS = 5V, VSYS = 8.4V, fSW = 1.5MHz, L=1µH\nISAT > IIN(max) + IRIPPLE/2 = 3.58A"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 72.6839 0)
		(size 38.1 16.2161)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ef3d39b3-2a4c-4978-aeae-8b9e36932fd6")
	)
